This definition captures a weaker notion of accuracy for proxim-
ity graphs compared to the standard recall metric. While Recall @𝑘
measures the fraction of the true 𝑘nearest neighbors retrieved, 𝜌𝛾
identifies the smallest 𝑘such that, with probability 𝛾,at least one of
the true𝑘nearest neighbors is returned by the search algorithm. A
good proximity graph induces a distribution 𝑝(𝑘)that puts higher
mass on smaller values of 𝑘, resulting in smaller recall bounds 𝜌𝛾.
Throughout our analysis, we fix a parameter 𝛾and derive bounds
parameterized by 𝜌𝛾. More generally, by varying 𝛾, one recovers
the full distribution 𝐹D,Gassociated with a proximity graph. Ad-
ditional details on recall bounds and the induced distributions are
provided in Appendix F. A graph with a larger value of 𝜌𝛾will show
worse query times when integrated with HENN, as also proved in
the following section.
